From 0c5212d9b10f561af62d936530727424c2811246 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 20:41:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild Navbar as responsive, animated, React-state-driven
 component

- Install framer-motion
- Replace the old classList.toggle('open')/getElementById DOM hacks
  with real React state (mobileOpen) and Framer Motion (AnimatePresence)
- Mobile menu: animated hamburger -> X, slide/fade panel, closes on
  link click, closes automatically if the viewport grows past the
  md breakpoint (e.g. rotating a tablet), locks body scroll while open
- Desktop services/products dropdown now animates in/out instead of
  popping, and Dropdown.js gets dark: variants + a proper list key
- Add proper aria-label/aria-expanded/aria-controls to the menu button
- Remove now-unused hamburger DOM-manipulation code from App.js and
  the matching hand-rolled CSS from App.css
